        {
          "kind": "sysSay",
          "line": "OH. Oh no. ...The gamblers are very quiet."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Valentina West is dead. You didn't ask. It knew."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "🕯️ Valentina West is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "What Valentina kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "\"Valentina's gone.\" Nathan looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Valentina.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Kanat blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 LEARNED: Calming Panic (Level 1). Ground them: 5 things you see, 4 you hear, 3 you touch. Breathe with them. Slow is fast."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\""
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 The Codex turns a page: Valentina West, 74 days. The mantle passes to Kanat Galymov."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "🪞 You wake up somebody else. Kanat Galymov, 28 — an emergency dispatcher. His hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Dowsing, War Cry, Scream Cheese."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "You knew Valentina — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "At the grave, Nathan, Pavel, Sofia and 1 more speak for Kanat — \"Valentina trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "The fire knew Kanat before the Codex did — his name already carried weight here."
        }
